<BaseLayout title="Infotainment">
  <h1>Infotainment</h1>
  <p>The 2021 S60 uses Volvo's Sensus-era center display and driver information systems. Screen size, audio hardware, navigation, head-up display, and connected services depend on installed options and market. Available functions depend on installed equipment, market, phone compatibility, and software version.</p>

  <h2>Displays and controls</h2>
  <figure class="reference-photo"><img src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img028459637a80b16dc0a801526df36585_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" alt="Volvo Sensus-era cockpit showing driver display, steering wheel and center touchscreen" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Volvo Sensus overview image. Optional display equipment varies by vehicle.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>Volvo's Sensus interface uses a center touchscreen, a digital driver display, and an optional head-up display. Not every vehicle has every display option. See <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/uk/support/car/s60/2020/article/f6848b197ef39a36c0a80151207886f7/">Volvo's Sensus overview</a> for the system layout and feature descriptions.</p>

  <h2>Center display</h2>
  <p>The center display provides access to vehicle settings, media, phone functions, climate controls, and supported connected features. Learn the home view, app view, and settings view while parked. Avoid navigating menus while the vehicle is moving.</p>

  <h2>Phone connection</h2>
  <p>For Bluetooth pairing, make the phone discoverable, open the vehicle's phone or Bluetooth settings, and follow the pairing prompts on both devices. Confirm the pairing code on both screens when requested. Menu wording may differ by software version.</p>

  <h2>Apple CarPlay and Android Auto</h2>
  <p>Phone integration availability and connection requirements should be checked against the equipment fitted to this particular car and the current phone software. Use a known-good data-capable USB cable when a wired connection is required; a charge-only cable will not carry data.</p>

  <h2>Audio and media</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Record the audio system name and speaker configuration from the vehicle's equipment/build information.</li>
    <li>Distinguish radio reception, Bluetooth audio, USB media, and phone-projection issues when troubleshooting.</li>
    <li>Check source volume and mute state before changing system settings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Software and troubleshooting notes</h2>
  <p>When documenting a display issue, record the software version, phone model and operating-system version, connection method, selected media source, and whether the issue repeats after a vehicle restart. Do not assume that a factory reset is the first or safest troubleshooting step.</p>

  <h2>Official information</h2>
  <p>Volvo provides the owner's information in the vehicle, online, and in downloadable formats. See <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/us/support/car/s60/20w46">Volvo S60 support</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
